---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Hona Financial" description="How Hona Financial collects, uses, stores and deletes your information.">
  <section class="band-cream on-cream">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,1.5rem+2.2vw,3rem)">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated August 2026</p>

      <p>
        Hona Financial ("Hona", "we", "our") is operated by Proprietary Solutions
        LLC. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your
        personal information. This policy explains what we collect, why, and what
        you can do about it.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account information — email address, and name and company name if you provide them</li>
        <li>Financial data you enter — receipts, projects, phases, categories, budgets and amounts</li>
        <li>Images you capture — receipt photographs and progress photographs</li>
        <li>Usage data — which features are used, and when</li>
        <li>Device information — operating system and app version</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide, maintain and improve the Hona application</li>
        <li>To store and organise your financial records</li>
        <li>To send account-related communications and support responses</li>
        <li>To send draw request notifications to the stakeholders you have granted access</li>
        <li>To process subscription payments</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>You own your data</h2>
      <p>
        Hona does not sell, rent or share your personal or financial data with
        third parties for marketing. We do not use your project data to train
        models. Your records are yours and you can export them at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing with stakeholders</h2>
      <p>
        When you grant a stakeholder — typically a lender — access to a project,
        they can see only what you have permitted: budgets, receipts, progress
        photographs and draw status, each governed by a separate permission you
        control. Access is scoped to the individual projects you share, is
        read-only apart from approving draw requests, and you can revoke it at
        any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party service providers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Stripe — payment processing</li>
        <li>Supabase — database and file storage</li>
        <li>Resend — transactional email delivery</li>
        <li>Google Cloud Vision — receipt text recognition</li>
        <li>Apple and Google — app distribution, and payment processing where you subscribe through an app store</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each provider operates under its own privacy policy and security standards.</p>

      <h2>Storage and security</h2>
      <p>
        Data is stored using encrypted infrastructure. Access to your records is
        enforced at the database level, not only in the application, so a request
        for data you do not own is refused by the database itself. Receipt images
        and progress photographs live in private storage and are served only
        through short-lived signed links to you and to stakeholders you have
        authorised.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        We retain your data for as long as your account is active. You can delete
        your account from within the app, under Administration. Deletion removes
        your projects, receipts, budgets, images, stakeholder grants and account
        record.
      </p>
      <p>
        One category is treated differently, deliberately. <strong>Records of draw
        requests are retained after deletion, with your identity removed.</strong>
        A lender approved those draws and released funds against them; erasing the
        record would remove evidence a third party relied on. What remains is the
        transaction — phase, amount, dates and status — with the personal
        identifiers stripped out. Nothing in a retained record identifies you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a payment record must be kept for tax or accounting obligations, we
        retain the minimum required and no more.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>At any time you may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request a copy of your data</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Delete your account and data from within the app</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise these rights, write to <a href="mailto:support@honafinancial.com">support@honafinancial.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>California residents</h2>
      <p>
        California residents have the right to know what personal information we
        collect, to request deletion, and to opt out of the sale of personal
        information. Hona does not sell personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Hona is not intended for anyone under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. Material changes will be communicated by email
        or in-app notice. Continued use constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:support@honafinancial.com">support@honafinancial.com</a><br />
        Proprietary Solutions LLC DBA Hona Financial<br />
        Queen Creek, Arizona
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
